   "summary": "Concluding section of the Akita Prefecture roster of Japanese educational institutions, covering elementary, secondary, vocational, youth, and special schools. It completes the catalog of public elementary schools with institutional data, founding dates, and enrollment and faculty counts as of April and November 1946. The document details private institutions including girls' vocational schools, Seirei Girls' High School, youth schools, and nineteen private nurseries and kindergartens. It also records specialized vocational and youth training institutes administered by non-educational ministries—including police, railway, and communications training centers—and Senshu School, a juvenile correction facility under the Ministry of Welfare.",
